---
description: Split work into separate commits so each change counts
alwaysApply: true
---

# Maximize contributions

When the user asks to commit or push, record the work as separate commits. One commit does one thing.

- Match this repo's history: a single imperative sentence about why the change exists.
- Keep each real change in its own commit instead of squashing the session into one.
- Include only the files that belong to that change.
- Do not create empty commits, rewrite dates, or split a change that cannot stand on its own.
- Push those commits to the requested branch. Do not force-push main.
